E_MA": 0.5500, "E_ND": 0.5000, "E_LoA": 0.7000, "E_mech": 0.1733, "muscle": "brachioradialis", "rationale": "Minor assistance to the isometric elbow hold; the near-neutral handle grip gives it reasonable leverage at the extended elbow angle.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 11.22, "fcsa_contribution_cm2": 1.94}, {"E_LT": 0.8500, "E_MA": 0.6000, "E_ND": 0.4500, "E_LoA": 0.4800, "E_mech": 0.1102, "muscle": "pectoralis_minor", "rationale": "Small mechanically necessary contribution to scapular anchoring; its depression action partly conflicts with the upward rotation the high finish requires.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 10.81, "fcsa_contribution_cm2": 1.19}], "effective_resistance": {"assumptions": ["Bilateral convention: 36 kg total is interpreted as 18 kg of stack per side.", "Representative commercial cable crossover / dual-adjustable pulley with a 2:1 ratio, so 18 kg of stack yields ~9 kg of handle force; ~92 N per hand after friction, ~184 N total.", "Single-joint shoulder movement: the near-straight arm gives a very large external moment arm, ~0.48 m from the GH joint to the cable line at the limiting phase.", "The cable force acts largely perpendicular to the forearm, creating an elbow EXTENSION moment; the elbow flexors work isometrically to hold the fixed elbow angle and transmit load from hand to humerus.", "Effective elbow external moment arm ~0.09 m per side; elbow flexor internal moment arm ~0.030 m at the near-extended elbow.", "Effective internal moment arm for combined humeral flexion/horizontal adduction ~0.054 m.", "Low-to-high vector: the required humeral moment combines flexion with horizontal adduction, favoring the clavicular pectoral fibres and anterior deltoid over the sternal head.", "Unsupported standing free-cable movement with no torso pad, so glenohumeral and scapular force transmission are mechanically required.", "Under the bilateral systemic convention the two mirrored cable lines cancel, so the anti-rotation trunk demand specific to the true single-arm 