a favorable length; part of its line of action is adduction rather than pure extension, slightly reducing alignment.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 105.22, "fcsa_contribution_cm2": 64.57}, {"E_LT": 0.9000, "E_MA": 0.8000, "E_ND": 0.8500, "E_LoA": 0.9500, "E_mech": 0.5814, "muscle": "semimembranosus", "rationale": "Large contributor to the hip extension moment; highly stretched at 90 degrees of hip flexion with a near-extended knee, so part of the resistance is supplied passively rather than by active force.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 88.78, "fcsa_contribution_cm2": 51.62}, {"E_LT": 0.9500, "E_MA": 0.8500, "E_ND": 0.9500, "E_LoA": 1.0000, "E_mech": 0.7671, "muscle": "latissimus_dorsi", "rationale": "Prime mover for the 182 N-m glenohumeral extension moment, well lengthened at the dead-stop bottom position; the required humeral action matches its line of pull almost exactly.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 43.85, "fcsa_contribution_cm2": 33.64}, {"E_LT": 0.9000, "E_MA": 0.8500, "E_ND": 0.9500, "E_LoA": 1.0000, "E_mech": 0.7268, "muscle": "brachialis", "rationale": "Largest elbow-flexion contributor and unaffected by forearm pronation, making it the dominant flexor against the 66 N-m elbow moment in a pronated row.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 44.05, "fcsa_contribution_cm2": 32.02}, {"E_LT": 0.8500, "E_MA": 0.8000, "E_ND": 0.8500, "E_LoA": 1.0000, "E_mech": 0.5780, "muscle": "wrist_flexors", "rationale": "Included as a mechanically necessary load-transmitting element: with a double-overhand grip and no straps, finger and wrist flexor force is the sole path by which the 1010 N reaches the arm, and each dead-stop rep re-establishes the grip.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 54.40, "fcsa_contribution_cm2": 31.44}, {"E_LT": 0.9000, "E_MA": 0.8000, "E_ND": 0.8500, "E_LoA": 0.9500, "E_mech": 0.5814, "muscle": "biceps_femoris_long_head", "rationale": "Shares the hip extension moment with the other hamstrings under the same stretched-length conditions.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 53.70, "fcsa_contribution_cm2": 31.22}, {"E_LT": 0.8500, "E_MA": 0.7500, "E_ND": 0.8500, "E_LoA": 0.9500, "E_mech": 0.5148, "muscle": "biceps_brachii", "rationale": "Meaningful elbow flexor, but the pronated grip reduces its effective flexion leverage and diverts part of its capacity into resisting the pronation moment.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 39.81, "fcsa_contribution_cm2": 20.49}, {"E_LT": 0.9000, "E_MA": 0.8500, "E_ND": 0.9000, "E_LoA": 1.0000, "E_mech": 0.6885, "muscle": "rhomboids", "rationale": "Scapular retraction is genuine task torque in a row, not mere stabilization: the scapula must be actively drawn back against a load pulling it into protraction and downward rotation.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 28.25, "fcsa_contribution_cm2": 19.45}, {"E_LT": 0.9000, "E_MA": 0.8500, "E_ND": 0.9000, "E_LoA": 1.0000, "E_mech": 0.6885, "muscle": "trapezius_middle", "rationale": "Primary horizontal scapular retractor, directly aligned with the required scapulothoracic moment.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 26.18, "fcsa_contribution_cm2": 18.03}, {"E_LT": 0.9000, "E_MA": 0.8500, "E_ND": 0.9000, "E_LoA": 0.9500, "E_mech": 0.6541, "muscle": "deltoid_posterior", "rationale": "Contributes shoulder extension and horizontal abduction as the elbow travels back; strongly aligned with the required humeral moment in the bent-over position.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 24.65, "fcsa_contribution_cm2": 16.12}, {"E_LT": 0.9000, "E_MA": 0.7500, "E_ND": 0.8500, "E_LoA": 0.9500, "E_mech": 0.5450, "muscle": "semitendinosus", "rationale": "Assists hip extension with a somewhat smaller internal moment arm than the other hamstrings.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 25.59, "fcsa_contribution_cm2": 13.95}, {"E_LT": 0.8500, "E_MA": 0.6000, "E_ND": 0.4000, "E_LoA": 0.3500, "E_mech": 0.0714, "muscle": "rotator_cuffs", "rationale": "Included as a mechanically necessary stabilizer: at the dead-stop bottom the full 1010 N acts as a distraction load on the hanging humerus, and cuff compression is required for that force to be transmitted into the scapula. Infraspinatus and teres minor add a small extension component.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 170.80, "fcsa_contribution_cm2": 12.20}, {"E_LT": 0.8500, "E_MA": 0.5500, "E_ND": 0.4500, "E_LoA": 0.5000, "E_mech": 0.1052, "muscle": "obliques", "rationale": "Included as a mechanically necessary load-transmitting element: with the lumbar extensors saturated, oblique-generated intra-abdominal pressure and thoracolumbar fascia tension carry a real share of the 470 N-m spinal moment. Most of the capacity is non-propulsive.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 81.71, "fcsa_contribution_cm2": 8.60}, {"E_LT": 0.8500, "E_MA": 0.8000, "E_ND": 0.8500, "E_LoA": 0.9000, "E_mech": 0.5202, "muscle": "trapezius_lower", "rationale": "Contributes retraction and resists the downward pull on the scapula in the horizontal-torso position.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 14.98, "fcsa_contribution_cm2": 7.79}, {"E_LT": 0.9000, "E_MA": 0.8000, "E_ND": 0.8500, "E_LoA": 0.9500, "E_mech": 0.5814, "muscle": "brachioradialis", "rationale": "Effective elbow flexor at the ~120 degree limiting angle, and the pronated grip does not penalize it as it does the biceps.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 11.22, "fcsa_contribution_cm2": 6.52}, {"E_LT": 0.8500, "E_MA": 0.7000, "E_ND": 0.7000, "E_LoA": 0.5500, "E_mech": 0.2291, "muscle": "trapezius_upper", "rationale": "Resists the scapula being pulled toward the floor by the suspended load; its elevation vector only partly matches the required retraction direction.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 19.36, "fcsa_contribution_cm2": 4.44}, {"E_LT": 0.9000, "E_MA": 0.6000, "E_ND": 0.5500, "E_LoA": 0.5500, "E_mech": 0.1634, "muscle": "transverse_abdominis", "rationale": "Primary generator of intra-abdominal pressure, which mechanically offloads part of the lumbar extension moment the erectors cannot fully cover.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 21.97, "fcsa_contribution_cm2": 3.59}, {"E_LT": 0.9500, "E_MA": 0.8500, "E_ND": 0.9000, "E_LoA": 1.0000, "E_mech": 0.7268, "muscle": "teres_major", "rationale": "Acts in parallel with latissimus dorsi on the humeral extension moment; small cross-section limits absolute contribution.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 4.50, "fcsa_contribution_cm2": 3.27}], "effective_resistance": {"assumptions": ["Barbell weight 883 N plus ~14% for the explosive dead-stop acceleration characteristic of the Pendlay variant: ~1010 N effective.", "Torso held ~15 degrees above horizontal, knees flexed ~20 degrees, bar starting under the shoulders.", "Horizontal distance hip joint to glenohumeral joint ~0.48 m; trunk, head and arm mass above the hip ~460 N acting at ~0.26 m.", "Horizontal distance L4/L5 to the bar line ~0.39 m; mass above L5 ~375 N at ~0.20 m.", "Forearms held near-vertical (~18 degrees off), giving an elbow external moment arm of ~0.065 m per side.", "Humerus length ~0.32 m: at 35 degrees of extension the glenohumeral external moment arm is ~0.18 m per side.", "Internal moment arms: latissimus shoulder extension ~0.06 m, elbow flexors ~0.040 m at 120 degrees, hip extensors ~0.055 m, erector spinae ~0.06 m.", "Approximately 30% of the lumbar moment is carried by intra-abdominal pressure and the posterior ligamentous/thoracolumbar fascia system rather than by active erector force.", "Approximately 40% of the hip extension moment is carried by passive hamstring and posterior capsule tension at ~90 degrees of hip flexion.", "Double-overhand pronated grip, no straps: grip force is mechanically required to transmit the entire 1010 N.", "The torso is unsupported, so the hip and lumbar extensor moments are load-bearing, not merely postural."], "loaded_joints": [{"joint": "hip_bilateral", "estimated_external_moment_nm": 605.00}, {"joint": "lumbar_spine", "estimated_external_moment_nm": 470.00}, {"joint": "glenohumeral_bilateral", "estimated_external_moment_nm": 182.00}, {"joint": "scapulothoracic_bilateral", "estimated_external_moment_nm": 70.00}, {"joint": "elbow_bilateral", "estimated_external_moment_nm": 66.00}], "nominal_load_kg": 90.00, "estimated_effective_force_n": 1010.00}, "systemic_fcsa_demand_cm2": 579.05, "top_down_fcsa_target_cm2": 578.00}
