46	seated_dumbbell_wrist_extension	Dumbbell Wrist Extension	Seated Palms-Down Dumbbell Wrist Extension	Upper	Forearms	Isolation	Dumbbell	12.00	38.37	{"wrist_extensors": 38.37}	{}	{}	{}	Unilateral	{"slug": "seated_dumbbell_wrist_extension", "notes": ["The contribution corresponds to approximately 7.67 Nm of bilateral wrist-extension capacity using a representative internal wrist-extensor moment arm near 0.0080 m.", "The 12 kg bilateral load is plausible for a strict 8-12 repetition set but requires substantially less absolute resistance than the palms-up wrist curl because the wrist extensors have lower practical force capacity.", "Wrist flexors are excluded because their net wrist-flexion action opposes the required movement; antagonist co-contraction is not counted as task-producing FCSA demand.", "Pronators and supinators are excluded because maintaining the palms-down orientation does not require them to produce a meaningful share of the external wrist-extension moment."], "limiting_phase": "Concentric initiation from moderate wrist flexion, with the forearms fully supported and the dumbbells producing their largest perpendicular moment about the wrist axes.", "reconciliation": "PASS", "vector_sum_cm2": 38.37, "muscle_evaluation": [{"E_LT": 0.9300, "E_MA": 0.8800, "E_ND": 0.9100, "E_LoA": 0.9600, "E_mech": 0.7150, "muscle": "wrist_extensors", "rationale": "The wrist-extensor aggregate directly generates the required net wrist-extension moment, with favorable starting length but a relatively small internal tendon moment arm.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 53.67, "fcsa_contribution_cm2": 38.37}], "effective_resistance": {"assumptions": ["The 12 kg nominal load represents two 6 kg dumbbells.", "The forearms remain fully supported on the thighs or a bench, minimizing meaningful elbow and shoulder loading.", "The combined perpendicular distance from the wrist axes to the dumbbell centres of mass is approximately 0.065 m at the limiting phase.", "The wrists begin in controlled 