32	kneeling_cable_crunch	Kneeling Cable Crunch	Kneeling Rope Cable Crunch	Core	Core	Isolation	Cable	60.00	45.59	{"obliques": 26.67, "rectus_abdominis": 18.92}	{}	{}	{}	Bilateral	{"slug": "kneeling_cable_crunch", "notes": ["The contribution vector generates approximately 59 Nm of thoracolumbar flexion capacity using representative effective internal moment arms of about 0.055 m for rectus abdominis and 0.050 m for the oblique aggregate.", "Iliopsoas is excluded because a strict cable crunch holds the hip angle relatively constant; meaningful hip-flexion contribution would indicate that the exercise had become a kneeling hip hinge.", "Latissimus dorsi and triceps are excluded because holding the rope and maintaining arm position do not generate a meaningful share of the required net thoracolumbar flexion moment.", "Transverse abdominis is excluded because its primary mechanical role is abdominal compression and segmental stabilization rather than production of a large net spinal-flexion moment.", "The estimate is sensitive to pulley ratio, kneeling distance from the stack, rope position, spinal range of motion, and the extent to which the hips remain fixed."], "limiting_phase": "Early-to-mid concentric spinal flexion from the extended or neutral starting position, before the cable line moves closer to the thoracolumbar flexion axis and the external moment declines.", "reconciliation": "PASS", "vector_sum_cm2": 45.59, "muscle_evaluation": [{"E_LT": 0.9000, "E_MA": 0.7800, "E_ND": 0.6200, "E_LoA": 0.7500, "E_mech": 0.3264, "muscle": "obliques", "rationale": "The bilateral oblique aggregate contributes substantial sagittal-plane trunk-flexion torque, although part of its anatomical capacity is oriented toward axial rotation and lateral flexion rather than pure flexion.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 81.71, "fcsa_contribution_cm2": 26.67}, {"E_LT": 0.9500, "E_MA": 0.9000, "E_ND": 0.9300, "E_LoA": 0.9800, "E_mech": 0.7793, "muscle": "rectus_abdominis", "rationale": "Acts as the most directly aligned thoracolumbar flexor and operates at favorable length and leverage near the initiation of the spinal-flexion phase.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 24.29, "fcsa_contribution_cm2": 18.92}], "effective_resistance": {"assumptions": ["A representative selectorized cable station with an approximately 0.90 effective stack-to-rope force ratio is assumed.", "The rope is held beside the head or upper chest, and the cable force acts with an effective perpendicular moment arm of approximately 0.112 m about the thoracolumbar flexion axis.", "The pelvis and hips remain substantially fixed while the thoracic and lumbar spine flex against the cable.", "The athlete avoids converting the movement into a kneeling hip hinge or forceful shoulder-extension exercise.", "The estimated cable force excludes meaningful momentum and assumes a controlled concentric repetition."], "loaded_joints": [{"joint": "thoracolumbar_flexion", "estimated_external_moment_nm": 59.33}], "nominal_load_kg": 60.00, "estimated_effective_force_n": 529.74}, "systemic_fcsa_demand_cm2": 45.59, "top_down_fcsa_target_cm2": 45.59}
