umed.", "The combined plate load, lever geometry, and approximately 12 kg of effective machine-arm and lower-limb weight produce about 1128 N of downward resistance at the forefeet.", "The effective external ankle moment arm is approximately 0.18 m from the ankle axes to the forefoot contact point.", "The knees remain flexed near 90 degrees, strongly shortening the gastrocnemius across the knee while leaving soleus force production largely available.", "The repetition begins from controlled dorsiflexion without bouncing or assistance from knee extension."], "loaded_joints": [{"joint": "ankle_plantar_flexion_bilateral", "estimated_external_moment_nm": 203.04}], "nominal_load_kg": 80.00, "estimated_effective_force_n": 1128.00}, "systemic_fcsa_demand_cm2": 162.70, "top_down_fcsa_target_cm2": 162.70}
