ation": "The seated hip position lengthens the long head, although its effective knee-flexion profile is somewhat less uniformly favorable than that of the medial hamstrings.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 37.17, "resistance_profile_alignment": "very_good", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "substantially_lengthened"}, {"H_m": 1.1500, "muscle": "semitendinosus", "etu_cm2": 22.22, "rationale": "Substantial lengthened tension through a broad controlled ROM provides a pronounced stretch-mediated advantage relative to conventional neutral dynamic tension.", "normalized_etu": 0.8683, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric"], "high_tension_rom": "broad", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 25.59, "smh_interpretation": "The hip-flexed position places the biarticular muscle at a long operating length while knee-flexion resistance remains substantial.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 19.32, "resistance_profile_alignment": "very_good", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "substantially_lengthened"}, {"H_m": 1.0000, "muscle": "biceps_femoris_short_head", "etu_cm2": 15.31, "rationale": "The muscle experiences conventional controlled dynamic tension through a substantial ROM without a clear positive or negative muscle-specific feature.", "normalized_etu": 0.6403, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric"], "high_tension_rom": "substantial", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 23.91, "smh_interpretation": "As a monoarticular knee flexor, the short head does not receive the hip-flexion-mediated lengthening advantage of the biarticular hamstrings.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 15.31, "resistance_profile_alignment": "good", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.9000, "muscle": "gastrocnemius", "etu_cm2": 2.27, "rationale": "The muscle receives meaningful but very low dynamic tension with a shortened-position bias and limited productive ROM, warranting a below-reference modifier.", "normalized_etu": 0.0124, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric"], "high_tension_rom": "limited", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 183.54, "smh_interpretation": "Knee flexion shortens the gastrocnemius proximally, and its very small contribution is not concentrated under favorable lengthened-loading conditions.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.52, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "moderate", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "shortened"}], "modifier_distribution": {"mode": 1.1500, "median": 1.1200, "maximum": 1.1500, "minimum": 0.9000, "unweighted_mean": 1.0640, "tension_weighted_mean": 1.1222}, "hypertrophic_quality_ratio": 1.1222, "active_tension_exposure_sum_cm2": 145.04}	{"gastrocnemius": 0.9500, "semitendinosus": 1.1500, "semimembranosus": 1.1500, "biceps_femoris_long_head": 1.1500, "biceps_femoris_short_head": 1.0500}	{"slug": "selectorized_seated_leg_curl", "notes": ["The exercise-defining recovery mechanism is the seated hip-flexed position: it places the biarticular hamstrings at long length before the repetition begins, and the eccentric extends the knee against a cam that maintains high resistance in exactly that lengthened region.", "This is one combined structural mechanism (high force x active lengthening x long muscle length), counted once at 1.15 rather than as separate eccentric and lengthened-position penalties.", "Biceps femoris short head is deliberately separated at 1.05 because it is monoarticular and does not inherit the hip-driven lengthening that distinguishes seated from prone leg curling.", "High tension fractions were not independently converted into large modifiers; that magnitude is already carried by Active Tension Exposure and contributes only a small nonlinear residual here.", "No stretch-mediated hypertrophy reasoning was applied — the elevation reflects persistent restoration of local force-producing capacity after lengthened-position loading, not hypertrophic quality."], "reconciliation": "PASS", "muscle_evaluation": [{"R_m": 1.1500, "muscle": "semimembranosus", "rationale": "The seated position holds the hip flexed, so the biarticular hamstring begins each repetition already lengthened, and the eccentric phase drives the knee toward extension while that hip flexion is maintained — the machine's cam keeps resistance high precisely in this most-lengthened position. This is the defining recovery mechanism: substantial active force coinciding with near-maximal muscle length produces a more persistent local force deficit than mid-range dynamic knee flexion. A tension fraction of 0.80 adds a small nonlinear residual cost. Lengthened-position loading and eccentric stress are treated as one combined structural mechanism, not two separate penalties, which caps the value at 1.15 rather than higher.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 88.78, "tension_fraction": 0.7966, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "high", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 70.72, "eccentric_structural_stress": "emphasized", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "none", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["high_force_active_lengthening_at_long_muscle_length", "high_relative_tension_nonlinear_residual"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "pronounced"}, {"R_m": 1.1500, "muscle": "biceps_femoris_long_head", "rationale": "Shares the exercise's defining mechanism: hip flexion fixed by the seat combines with knee extension during the eccentric to load the long head at a substantially lengthened position under high machine-supplied force. This interaction of high force with active lengthening at long length is the specific reason for the elevation; tension fraction of 0.69 contributes a minor additional nonlinear component.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 53.70, "tension_fraction": 0.6922, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "high", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 37.17, "eccentric_structural_stress": "emphasized", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "none", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["high_force_active_lengthening_at_long_muscle_length", "high_relative_tension_nonlinear_residual"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "pronounced"}, {"R_m": 1.1500, "muscle": "semitendinosus", "rationale": "As a biarticular hamstring it experiences the same seated-position lengthening at the hip plus loaded knee extension during the eccentric, with its long fascicles subjected to high force at extended length. This produces persistent rather than merely acute impairment of force-producing readiness, justifying the same elevation as the other biarticular hamstrings.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 25.59, "tension_fraction": 0.7550, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "high", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 19.32, "eccentric_structural_stress": "emphasized", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "none", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["high_force_active_lengthening_at_long_muscle_length", "high_relative_tension_nonlinear_residual"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "pronounced"}, {"R_m": 1.0500, "muscle": "biceps_femoris_short_head", "rationale": "Monoarticular and therefore unaffected by the seated hip flexion that lengthens the other hamstrings; its length is set by knee angle alone, so its lengthened-position exposure is limited to knee extension under load. That still constitutes mild loaded lengthening beyond the mid-range reference, warranting a small elevation but clearly less than the biarticular heads.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 23.91, "tension_fraction": 0.6403, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "high", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 15.31, "eccentric_structural_stress": "standard", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "none", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["loaded_eccentric_at_moderately_lengthened_knee_position", "conventional_contractile_fatigue"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "mild"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "gastrocnemius", "rationale": "Assists knee flexion only marginally, at low force and with the ankle held in a fixed position by the footplate, so it is not driven through loaded lengthening. Its tension unloads fully between repetitions and leaves little persistent local deficit, placing it slightly below the dynamic reference.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 183.54, "tension_fraction": 0.0137, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.52, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "intermittent", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["low_level_synergist_isometric_tension"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}], "modifier_distribution": {"mode": 1.1500, "median": 1.1500, "maximum": 1.1500, "minimum": 0.9500, "unweighted_mean": 1.0900, "tension_weighted_mean": 1.1360}, "standardized_repetition": {"tempo": "controlled conventional tempo", "range_of_motion": "full intended ROM", "proximity_to_failure": "effective repetition"}, "active_tension_exposure_sum_cm2": 145.04}	{"hip_joint": 0.1000, "tibiofemoral_joint": 0.7800, "patellofemoral_joint": 0.0800}	{"slug": "selectorized_seated_leg_curl", "notes": ["This is primarily a tibiofemoral knee-flexion exercise; machine guidance reduces stabilization requirements without eliminating high local joint moment and hamstring-force transmission.", "Patellofemoral exposure remains low because substantial quadriceps-generated patellofemoral compression is absent."], "loaded_joints": ["tibiofemoral_joint", "hip_joint", "patellofemoral_joint"], "reconciliation": "PASS", "joint_evaluation": [{"joint": "tibiofemoral_joint", "rationale": "The tibiofemoral joint is the primary loaded articulation. The 50 kg machine resistance creates a large external knee-extension moment that must be opposed by high hamstring knee-flexion force. Those muscle forces generate substantial tibiofemoral compression together with posteriorly directed tibial shear, while meaningful loading persists through progressively greater knee flexion. Machine guidance limits stabilization demand but does not materially reduce the large local knee-flexion moment and internal joint forces.", "load_exposure": 0.7800, "loaded_joint_position": "demanding", "primary_loading_modes": ["net_joint_moment", "compression", "shear", "muscle_force_transmission"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "high", "stabilization_requirement": "low", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "moderate", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "high"}, {"joint": "hip_joint", "rationale": "The hip remains substantially flexed and the biarticular hamstrings transmit force across it, producing limited hip-joint compression and force transmission. However, the pelvis and thigh are externally supported and the exercise imposes little direct hip moment, so hip exposure remains secondary.", "load_exposure": 0.1000, "loaded_joint_position": "demanding", "primary_loading_modes": ["muscle_force_transmission"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "minimal", "stabilization_requirement": "minimal", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "minimal", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "low"}, {"joint": "patellofemoral_joint", "rationale": "Knee flexion changes patellofemoral contact geometry and produces some compressive exposure, but the exercise does not require substantial quadriceps force. Consequently, patellofemoral loading is small relative to knee-extension exercises despite the flexed-knee position.", "load_exposure": 0.0800, "loaded_joint_position": "demanding", "primary_loading_modes": ["compression"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "minimal", "stabilization_requirement": "minimal", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "minimal", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "low"}], "maximum_exposure_joint": "tibiofemoral_joint", "standardized_repetition": {"tempo": "controlled conventional tempo", "range_of_motion": "full intended ROM", "proximity_to_failure": "effective repetition"}}
