ain at the neutral reference because they combine productive dynamic trunk flexion with stabilizing control.", "Deep abdominal, hip, spinal-extensor, grip, and elbow-position contributions receive reduced modifiers because they are predominantly isometric, accessory, or low-ROM.", "ETU values equal active tension exposure multiplied by the listed H_m values within rounding tolerance."], "etu_sum_cm2": 53.97, "reconciliation": "PASS", "muscle_evaluation": [{"H_m": 1.0000, "muscle": "obliques", "etu_cm2": 26.67, "rationale": "The muscle group receives conventional dynamic concentric and eccentric tension through substantial trunk-flexion ROM. Its simultaneous bracing role does not independently raise or lower the reference modifier.", "normalized_etu": 0.3264, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric", "isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "substantial", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 81.71, "smh_interpretation": "The obliques shorten dynamically during spinal flexion while also maintaining transverse- and frontal-plane control, producing a mixture of productive excursion and bracing.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 26.67, "resistance_profile_alignment": "good", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 1.0500, "muscle": "rectus_abdominis", "etu_cm2": 19.87, "rationale": "Broad controlled dynamic tension beginning from a moderately lengthened trunk position provides a modest advantage over neutral reference loading, but not a pronounced stretch-mediated case.", "normalized_etu": 0.8180, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric"], "high_tension_rom": "broad", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 24.29, "smh_interpretation": "The cable maintains trunk-flexion demand from the relatively extended upper position through a broad spinal-flexion range, providing useful tension before the muscle becomes strongly shortened.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 18.92, "resistance_profile_alignment": "good", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sus