_isometric_tension"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "erector_spinae", "rationale": "Acts only as a low-force antagonist controlling segmental spinal position; the tension is intermittent, submaximal and not applied at a lengthened position under meaningful load, so it leaves little persistent force deficit.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 106.48, "tension_fraction": 0.0141, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.50, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "intermittent", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["low_level_antagonist_co_contraction"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "wrist_flexors", "rationale": "Light grip on the rope produces submaximal isometric tension with no lengthening and no perfusion-limiting force; the resulting fatigue resolves rapidly and contributes little persistent deficit.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 54.40, "tension_fraction": 0.0276, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.50, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "intermittent", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["low_level_gripping_isometric_tension"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "brachialis", "rationale": "Holds elbow angle constant at very low force to keep the rope fixed against the head; there is no dynamic excursion and no loaded lengthening, so persistent recovery cost per unit tension falls slightly below the dynamic reference.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 44.05, "tension_fraction": 0.0227, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_e