d transfers force between the shoulder girdle, pelvis, and supported leg without allowing trunk deformation.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 21.97, "mechanical_roles": ["trunk_bracing", "isometric_fixation", "load_transmission"], "tension_fraction": 0.1365, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 3.00, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "rectus_abdominis", "rationale": "Maintains ribcage-to-pelvis alignment and limits lumbar extension while the obliques resist lateral flexion and rotation.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 24.29, "mechanical_roles": ["trunk_bracing", "isometric_fixation", "antagonist_co_contraction"], "tension_fraction": 0.1029, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.50, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "rotator_cuffs", "rationale": "Centres the humeral head of the supporting arm while bodyweight is transmitted through the shoulder. Forearm and bench support keep the required cuff fraction relatively low.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 170.80, "mechanical_roles": ["joint_stabilization", "load_transmission", "isometric_fixation"], "tension_fraction": 0.0146, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.50, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "serratus_anterior", "rationale": "Maintains scapular contact with the thorax and supports load transfer through the planted forearm and shoulder.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 36.03, "mechanical_roles": ["scapular_control", "load_transmission", "isometric_fixation"], "tension_fraction": 0.0555, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.00, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "deltoid_lateral", "rationale": "Contributes low-level shoulder-abduction and compression force to maintain the supporting upper arm beneath the torso.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 45.73, "mechanical_roles": ["joint_stabilization", "load_transmission", "isometric_fixation"], "tension_fraction": 0.0328, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.50, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "erector_spinae", "rationale": "Co-contracts with the abdominal wall to maintain neutral spinal alignment and prevent flexion or rotation during the side-plank hold.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 106.48, "mechanical_roles": ["trunk_bracing", "antagonist_co_contraction", "isometric_fixation"], "tension_fraction": 0.0141, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.50, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "gluteus_minimus", "rationale": "Provides low-level femoral-head and pelvic stabilization alongside the gluteus medius while the adductors bear the principal load.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 24.82, "mechanical_roles": ["joint_stabilization", "limb_position_maintenance", "isometric_fixation"], "tension_fraction": 0.0483, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.20, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "triceps_lateral_head", "rationale": "Maintains the supporting elbow position and transfers force through the upper arm, although forearm support substantially reduces elbow-extension demand.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 36.10, "mechanical_roles": ["isometric_fixation", "load_transmission", "limb_position_maintenance"], "tension_fraction": 0.0277, "pro