ment": "poor", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "moderate", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8500, "muscle": "gluteus_minimus", "etu_cm2": 1.02, "rationale": "The exposure is mechanically specific but predominantly isometric and accessory.", "normalized_etu": 0.0411, "contraction_mode": ["isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 24.82, "smh_interpretation": "The muscle assists hip and pelvic stabilization without dynamic abduction or rotation through a substantial range.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.20, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "moderate", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8500, "muscle": "triceps_lateral_head", "etu_cm2": 0.85, "rationale": "The muscle performs low-level positional tension without dynamic elbow-extension excursion.", "normalized_etu": 0.0235, "contraction_mode": ["isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 36.10, "smh_interpretation": "The elbow remains fixed while support force is transmitted through the forearm and upper arm.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.00, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "moderate", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}], "modifier_distribution": {"mode": 0.8500, "median": 0.8500, "maximum": 0.9000, "minimum": 0.8000, "unweighted_mean": 0.8458, "tension_weighted_mean": 0.8812}, "hypertrophic_quality_ratio": 0.8812, "active_tension_exposure_sum_cm2": 150.72}	{"obliques": 1.0000, "rotator_cuffs": 0.9500, "erector_spinae": 0.9500, "gluteus_medius": 0.9500, "adductor_magnus": 1.1000, "deltoid_lateral": 0.9500, "gluteus_minimus": 0.9500, "rectus_abdominis": 0.9500, "serratus_anterior": 0.9500, "transverse_abdominis": 0.9500, "triceps_lateral_head": 0.9500, "adductor_longus_brevis": 1.1000}	{"slug": "copenhagen_plank", "notes": ["This is the specific case in which the isometry guidance permits a meaningful penalty: the adductors sustain high force at a lengthened hip-abducted position with materially restricted perfusion and no unloading phase, making a residual post-exercise force deficit plausible rather than purely intra-set fatigue.", "Sustained tension and lengthened-position loading were combined into one mechanism for the adductors rather than counted as two full penalties, which is why the value stops at 1.10.", "Obliques were placed at the neutral reference rather than elevated: their hold is continuous but near neutral muscle length and at moderate force, so it does not meet the threshold for a persistent-deficit mechanism.", "All remaining shoulder, scapular, trunk and hip stabilizers operate at low force relative to their available capacity, which the specification treats as having little effect on R_m; they received 0.95 despite the continuous duty cycle.", "The exercise's reputation for adductor strain prevention and its high perceived difficulty were excluded; only local persistent recovery cost per unit tension was estimated."], "reconciliation": "PASS", "muscle_evaluation": [{"R_m": 1.1000, "muscle": "adductor_magnus", "rationale": "The bench-supported position holds the hip abducted, so the adductors sustain high force while already substantially lengthened, and unlike ordinary postural isometry there is no unloading phase whatsoever within the effort. The combination of sustained near-continuous tension, materially restricted local perfusion, and the lengthened position under load makes a residual post-exercise force deficit plausible rather than merely severe intra-set fatigue, which is what justifies the elevation. It is capped at 1.10 because much isometric fatigue does resolve on release and the sustained-tension and lengthened-position factors are treated as one combined mechanism rather than two full penalties.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 105.22, "tension_fraction": 0.5455, "perfusion_constraint": "high", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "substantial", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 57.40, "eccentric_structural_stress": "standard", "meaningful_tension_duration": "continuous", "sustained_isometric_tension": "sustained", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["sustained_high_force_isometry_at_lengthened_adductor_position", "perfusion_constrained_tension_with_no_unloading_phase"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "moderate"}, {"R_m": 1.1000, "muscle": "adductor_longus_brevis", "rationale": "Shares the defining mechanism: the short adductors are held near end-range abduction while bearing the supported limb and trunk load continuously, with no phase in which tension releases. A tension fraction of 0.65 adds a small nonlinear residual cost of operating close to available capacity. The persistent component of this exposure exceeds ordinary dynamic tension, warranting the same clearly elevated value as adductor magnus.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 66.55, "tension_fraction": 0.6546, "perfusion_constraint": "high", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "high", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 43.56, "eccentric_structural_stress": "standard", "meaningful_tension_duration": "continuous", "sustained_isometric_tension": "sustained", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["sustained_high_force_isometry_at_lengthened_adductor_position", "perfusion_constrained_tension_with_no_unloading_phase", "high_relative_tension_nonlinear_residual"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "moderate"}, {"R_m": 1.0000, "muscle": "obliques", "rationale": "Holds the trunk against lateral collapse continuously with no unloading phase, which lifts it above the sub-reference value given to intermittent stabilizing tension. However, the trunk is held near neutral length rather than in a loaded lengthened position, and moderate-force isometric fatigue of this type recovers substantially once tension is released, so the neutral reference rather than an elevated value is the appropriate estimate.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 81.71, "tension_fraction": 0.3740, "perfusion_constraint": "moderate", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "moderate", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 30.56, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "continuous", "sustained_isometric_tension": "sustained", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["sustained_lateral_anti_gravity_isometry"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "gluteus_medius", "rationale": "Contributes frontal-plane hip control on the supported side at low force relative to its large available capacity; the tension is not applied at a lengthened position and generates fatigue that resolves largely on release, so persistent cost sits just below the dynamic reference despite the continuous duty cycle.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 113.75, "tension_fraction": 0.0352, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 4.00, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "continuous", "sustained_isometric_tension": "sustained", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["low_level_sustained_stabilizing_isometric_tension"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "transverse_abdominis", "rationale": "Maintains intra-abdominal pressure at low force throughout the hold with no contractile lengthening under load; such low-level bracing produces predominantly transient fatigue and leaves little persistent local deficit.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 21.97, "tension_fraction": 0.1366, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 3.00, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "continuous", "sustained_isometric_tension": "sustained", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["low_level_bracing_isometric_tension"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "rotator_cuffs", "rationale": "Stabilises the down-side glenohumeral joint at very low force relative to its available capacity, without lengthening under meaningful load; the resulting fatigue resolves on release rather than persisting.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 170.80, "tension_fraction": 0.0146, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.50, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "continuous", "sustained_isometric_tension": "sustained", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["low_level_sustained_stabilizing_isometric_tension"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "rectus_abdominis", "rationale": "Provides low-force anti-extension bracing in the side-lying position; the muscle is neither lengthened under load nor highly loaded, so its persistent recovery component sits marginally below the dynamic reference.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 24.29, "tension_fraction": 0.1029, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.50, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "continuous", "sustained_isometric_tension": "sustained", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["low_level_bracing_isometric_tension"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "serratus_anterior", "rationale": "Holds the scapula against the thorax on the supporting side at low force with no loaded lengthening; sustained tension of this magnitude leaves little persistent force deficit relative to dynamic loading.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 36.03, "tension_fraction": 0.0555, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.00, "eccentric_struct