tributions receive 0.85 because their exposure is sustained but predominantly isometric.", "The rotator cuffs and transverse abdominis receive the minimum modifier because their exposure consists almost entirely of low-ROM joint stabilization or deep trunk bracing.", "No muscle receives a modifier above 0.90 because the Pallof press intentionally minimizes trunk and pelvic movement and therefore provides little productive muscle-length excursion.", "ETU values equal active tension exposure multiplied by the listed H_m values within rounding tolerance."], "etu_sum_cm2": 76.94, "reconciliation": "PASS", "muscle_evaluation": [{"H_m": 0.9000, "muscle": "obliques", "etu_cm2": 25.20, "rationale": "The obliques sustain high, specific anti-rotation tension with controlled force changes during the press-out and return. Predominantly isometric function and limited fibre excursion keep the modifier below the dynamic reference.", "normalized_etu": 0.3084, "contraction_mode": ["isometric", "concentric", "eccentric"], "high_tension_rom": "limited", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 81.71, "smh_interpretation": "The cable creates a direct and increasing anti-rotation moment as the arms extend, but the obliques are intended to preserve nearly fixed trunk geometry.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 28.00, "resistance_profile_alignment": "very_good", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8500, "muscle": "rectus_abdominis", "etu_cm2": 8.08, "rationale": "The bracing demand is meaningful and sustained but predominantly isometric and low-ROM.", "normalized_etu": 0.3326, "contraction_mode": ["isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 24.29, "smh_interpretation": "The rectus abdominis maintains ribcage-to-pelvis alignment without dynamic spinal flexion.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 9.50, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mi