rce lengthening mechanism applies.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 25.59, "tension_fraction": 0.0782, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.00, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "intermittent", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["low_level_antagonist_co_contraction"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "biceps_femoris_short_head", "rationale": "Contributes minimal knee-flexor co-contraction for joint stability at very low force, with no loaded lengthening; the fatigue produced is transient.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 23.91, "tension_fraction": 0.0836, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.00, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "intermittent", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["low_level_antagonist_co_contraction"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}], "modifier_distribution": {"mode": 0.9500, "median": 0.9500, "maximum": 1.0500, "minimum": 0.9500, "unweighted_mean": 0.9700, "tension_weighted_mean": 0.9979}, "standardized_repetition": {"tempo": "controlled conventional tempo", "range_of_motion": "full intended ROM", "proximity_to_failure": "effective repetition"}, "active_tension_exposure_sum_cm2": 266.82}	{"hip_joint": 0.0800, "tibiofemoral_joint": 0.6800, "patellofemoral_joint": 0.8600}	{"slug": "selectorized_leg_extension", "notes": ["The exercise is dominated by quadriceps-generated knee-extension loading.", "Patellofemoral exposure exceeds tibiofemoral exposure because high quadriceps force is transmitted directly through the extensor mechanism and produces substantial patellofemoral compression.", "The selectorized machine reduces stabilization requirements without materially reducing direct knee-joint loading."], "loaded_joints": ["patellofemoral_joint", "tibiofemoral_joint", "hip_joint"], "reconciliation": "PASS", "joint_evaluation": [{"joint": "patellofemoral_joint", "rationale": "The patellofemoral joint is the most heavily exposed articulation. The 60 kg selectorized resistance creates a large external knee-flexion moment that must be opposed by high quadriceps force. That force is transmitted through the quadriceps tendon, patella, and patellar tendon, producing substantial patellofemoral reaction and compression across the loaded knee-extension ROM. Relative to conventional resistance exercises, seated leg extension is among the more mechanically demanding direct patellofemoral loading patterns.", "load_exposure": 0.8600, "loaded_joint_position": "demanding", "primary_loading_modes": ["net_joint_moment", "compression", "muscle_force_transmission"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "very_high", "stabilization_requirement": "low", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "low", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "very_high"}, {"joint": "tibiofemoral_joint", "rationale": "The tibiofemoral joint experiences a large knee-extension moment and substantial quadriceps-generated joint reaction force. Open-chain knee extension also creates meaningful anterior-posterior shear components whose magnitude and direction vary with knee angle. The machine constrains the motion path and minimizes stabilization demand, but the local knee moment and internal force remain substantial.", "load_exposure": 0.6800, "loaded_joint_position": "mid_range", "primary_loading_modes": ["net_joint_moment", "compression", "shear", "muscle_force_transmission"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "high", "stabilization_requirement": "low", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "moderate", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "high"}, {"joint": "hip_joint", "rationale": "The hip remains flexed and the rectus femoris spans the joint, so some force is transmitted proximally. However, the pelvis and thigh are externally supported and there is little direct hip moment, leaving hip exposure minor relative to the knee.", "load_exposure": 0.0800, "loaded_joint_position": "demanding", "primary_loading_modes": ["muscle_force_transmission"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "minimal", "stabilization_requirement": "minimal", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "minimal", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "low"}], "maximum_exposure_joint": "patellofemoral_joint", "standardized_repetition": {"tempo": "controlled conventional tempo", "range_of_motion": "full intended ROM", "proximity_to_failure": "effective repetition"}}
