elvis and prevents hip flexion under the barbell moment while transmitting force from the lower body into the trunk. The supplied value already represents this large isometric demand.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 143.08, "mechanical_roles": ["isometric_fixation", "load_transmission", "trunk_bracing"], "tension_fraction": 0.7268, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 103.99, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 103.99, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "erector_spinae", "rationale": "Produces near-maximal spinal-extension tension to hold the torso approximately horizontal against the large flexion moment created by the bar. The supplied value is retained as the complete force state.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 106.48, "mechanical_roles": ["trunk_bracing", "isometric_fixation", "load_transmission"], "tension_fraction": 0.9025, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 96.10, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 96.10, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "adductor_magnus", "rationale": "Its posterior fibres assist the gluteus maximus in resisting hip flexion and stabilizing the femur and pelvis in the hinged stance. The supplied value plausibly captures this substantial static hip-extension demand.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 105.22, "mechanical_roles": ["isometric_fixation", "load_transmission", "limb_position_maintenance"], "tension_fraction": 0.6137, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 64.57, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 64.57, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "semimembranosus", "rationale": "Resists hip flexion while helping maintain the slightly flexed knee and stable pelvis. The supplied contribution already combines its hip-extension and biarticular fixation roles.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 88.78, "mechanical_roles": ["isometric_fixation", "load_transmission", "multi_joint_control"], "tension_fraction": 0.5814, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 51.62, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 51.62, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "latissimus_dorsi", "rationale": "Generates shoulder-extension torque to pull the humerus toward the torso and controls the bar's descent. The supplied value represents its complete dynamic force state.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 43.85, "mechanical_roles": ["propulsive", "load_transmission", "eccentric_control"], "tension_fraction": 0.7672, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 33.64, "contraction_character": ["dynamic_concentric", "dynamic_eccentric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 33.64, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_propulsive"}, {"muscle": "brachialis", "rationale": "Produces substantial elbow-flexion torque during the pull and eccentrically controls elbow extension as the bar returns to the floor. No additional fixation component is added separately.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 44.05, "mechanical_roles": ["propulsive", "eccentric_control"], "tension_fraction": 0.7269, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 32.02, "contraction_character": ["dynamic_concentric", "dynamic_eccentric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 32.02, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_propulsive"}, {"muscle": "wrist_flexors", "rationale": "Maintains the closed pronated grip and transmits the full bar load through the hand. The supplied value already reflects the high grip demand and is retained.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 54.40, "mechanical_roles": ["grip_maintenance", "isometric_fixation", "load_transmission"], "tension_fraction": 0.5779, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 31.44, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 31.44, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "biceps_femor