mary loaded articulation. The 80 kg cable resistance creates substantial shoulder-flexion and horizontal-adduction moments that must be opposed during shoulder extension and horizontal abduction. The wide grip increases the horizontal-abduction component and keeps the humeri farther from the torso, increasing posterior-deltoid, rotator-cuff, and associated shoulder-force demand. High muscle force produces meaningful glenohumeral compression and translational control, while the cable path provides more external constraint than free dumbbells or a barbell.", "load_exposure": 0.7000, "loaded_joint_position": "demanding", "primary_loading_modes": ["net_joint_moment", "compression", "translation", "muscle_force_transmission", "stabilization"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "high", "stabilization_requirement": "moderate", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "moderate", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "high"}, {"joint": "scapulothoracic_articulation", "rationale": "The wide-grip row requires substantial scapular retraction and controlled protraction through the return phase. Middle trapezius, rhomboids, posterior shoulder musculature, and associated scapular stabilizers transmit large cable forces between the upper limbs and thorax. The wide grip emphasizes scapular retraction mechanics relative to narrower rowing variants, producing substantial functional scapulothoracic exposure.", "load_exposure": 0.6200, "loaded_joint_position": "mid_range", "primary_loading_modes": ["net_joint_moment", "muscle_force_transmission", "stabilization"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "high", "stabilization_requirement": "moderate", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "low", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "high"}, {"joint": "elbow_joint", "rationale": "The elbow flexors must overcome a substantial external extension moment as the cable is pulled toward the torso. Brachialis, brachioradialis, and biceps generate meaningful joint reaction and compression. Exposure remains substantial but is somewhat lower than in narrower neutral-grip rows or direct curls because the wide grip shifts a larger share of the pulling task toward shoulder horizontal abduction and scapular retraction.", "load_exposure": 0.6000, "loaded_joint_position": "mid_range", "primary_loading_modes": ["net_joint_moment", "compression", "muscle_force_transmission"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "high", "stabilization_requirement": "low", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "low", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "high"}, {"joint": "acromioclavicular_joint", "rationale": "Substantial scapular retraction under cable resistance requires force transmission through the scapula-clavicle interface. This creates meaningful but secondary AC-joint exposure, without the high elevation, compression, or overhead rotational demand seen in pressing and overhead-loading exercises.", "load_exposure": 0.2200, "loaded_joint_position": "mid_range", "primary_loading_modes": ["muscle_force_transmission", "stabilization"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "low", "stabilization_requirement": "moderate", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "low", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "moderate"}, {"joint": "radiocarpal_joint", "rationale": "The wrists mainly transmit grip force while remaining approximately neutral on the wide handle. Forearm musculature must stabilize the hands against substantial cable tension, but direct wrist flexion-extension or deviation moment remains limited.", "load_exposure": 0.1600, "loaded_joint_position": "favorable", "primary_loading_modes": ["muscle_force_transmission", "stabilization"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "low", "stabilization_requirement": "low", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "low", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "moderate"}, {"joint": "lumbar_spine", "rationale": "The seated position substantially reduces lower-body and spinal loading compared with unsupported rows. The lumbar spine still provides isometric trunk stabilization against the horizontal cable force, but with technically valid execution and limited torso swing the external trunk moment remains small.", "load_exposure": 0.1200, "loaded_joint_position": "favorable", "primary_loading_modes": ["stabilization", "compression"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "low", "stabilization_requirement": "moderate", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "minimal", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "low"}], "maximum_exposure_joint": "glenohumeral_joint", "standardized_repetition": {"tempo": "controlled conventional tempo", "range_of_motion": "full intended ROM", "proximity_to_failure": "effective repetition"}}
