he middle of the curl and declines toward the top.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 32.98, "resistance_profile_alignment": "good", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "moderately_lengthened"}, {"H_m": 1.0000, "muscle": "biceps_brachii", "etu_cm2": 27.87, "rationale": "Strong line-of-pull alignment and broad dynamic ROM support reference-quality exposure, but the standing curl lacks the shoulder-extension lengthening of an incline curl.", "normalized_etu": 0.7001, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric"], "high_tension_rom": "broad", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 39.81, "smh_interpretation": "The supinated grip aligns strongly with the biceps, but the neutral shoulder position and bell-shaped free-weight torque profile do not create exceptional long-length loading.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 27.87, "resistance_profile_alignment": "good", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "moderately_lengthened"}, {"H_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "brachioradialis", "etu_cm2": 6.51, "rationale": "Useful dynamic elbow-flexion tension is present, but the supinated forearm orientation reduces mechanical alignment relative to hammer-style curling.", "normalized_etu": 0.5802, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric"], "high_tension_rom": "substantial", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 11.22, "smh_interpretation": "The muscle flexes the elbow dynamically from near extension, but the fully supinated barbell grip is less favorable than a neutral-grip configuration.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 6.85, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "moderately_lengthened"}, {"H_m": 0.9000, "muscle": "deltoid_anterior", "etu_cm2": 5.45, "rationale": "Some dynamic shoulder contribution may occur, but limited excursion and a substantial positional component keep the modifier below the neutral reference.", "normalized_etu": 0.1789, "c