e wrist extensors stabilize a nearly fixed wrist rather than producing dynamic extension through a meaningful ROM.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.50, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8000, "muscle": "transverse_abdominis", "etu_cm2": 2.00, "rationale": "Low-ROM postural bracing provides distinctly lower hypertrophic tension quality than conventional dynamic resistance exercise.", "normalized_etu": 0.0910, "contraction_mode": ["isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 21.97, "smh_interpretation": "The muscle braces the abdominal wall without meaningful dynamic shortening or lengthening under load.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.50, "resistance_profile_alignment": "poor", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8500, "muscle": "pronators_supinators", "etu_cm2": 1.70, "rationale": "Forearm-orientation fixation is mechanically specific but predominantly isometric and low-ROM.", "normalized_etu": 0.0279, "contraction_mode": ["isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 60.88, "smh_interpretation": "The forearm remains close to a fixed rotational position, producing little loaded excursion.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.00, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "moderate", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8500, "muscle": "trapezius_lower", "etu_cm2": 1.70, "rationale": "Its mixed dynamic and stabilizing tension is meaningful but occurs through limited excursion and at low absolute load.", "normalized_etu": 0.1135, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric", "isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "limited", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 14.98, "smh_interpretation": "The lower trapezius participates in scapular rotation and tilt but remains primarily a controller rather than a dynamically overloaded mover.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.00, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8500, "muscle": "brachioradialis", "etu_cm2": 1.65, "rationale": "The muscle experiences substantial fixation tension relative to its size, but muscle size does not raise H_m and the predominantly isometric character remains below reference quality.", "normalized_etu": 0.1471, "contraction_mode": ["isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 11.22, "smh_interpretation": "The elbow remains nearly fixed, so the muscle is loaded without substantial shortening or lengthening.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.94, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8000, "muscle": "erector_spinae", "etu_cm2": 1.60, "rationale": "Low-level postural fixation with little loaded ROM represents distinctly low-quality hypertrophic tension.", "normalized_etu": 0.0150, "contraction_mode": ["isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 106.48, "smh_interpretation": "The spinal extensors maintain posture with minimal productive excursion.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.00, "resistance_profile_alignment": "poor", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8500, "muscle": "pectoralis_minor", "etu_cm2": 1.28, "rationale": "The tension is mechanically meaningful but predominantly stabilizing and low-ROM.", "normalized_etu": 0.1184, "contraction_mode": ["isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "limited", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 10.81, "smh_interpretation": "The muscle contributes mainly to scapular fixation and protraction control without broad dynamic excursion.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.50, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "moderate", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8000, "muscle": "trapezius_middle", "etu_cm2": 1.20, "rationale": "Incidental antagonist braking and fixation with little productive excursion warrant the lower calibration anchor.", "normalized_etu": 0.0458, "contraction_mode": ["isometric", "eccentric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 26.18, "smh_interpretation": "The middle trapezius primarily brakes protraction and maintains scapular position rather than performing loaded retraction.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.50, "resistance_profile_alignment": "poor", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "moderate", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8000, "muscle": "trapezius_upper", "etu_cm2": 0.80, "rationale": "The exposure is low-level, accessory, and dominated by postural scapular control rather than productive dynamic loading.", "normalized_etu": 0.0413, "contraction_mode": ["isometric", "concentric", "eccentric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 19.36, "smh_interpretation": "The muscle contributes only low-level clavicular and scapular control and is not loaded through a substantial shrugging ROM.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.00, "resistance_profile_alignment": "poor", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "moderate", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}], "modifier_distribution": {"mode": 0.8500, "median": 0.8500, "maximum": 1.1000, "minimum": 0.8000, "unweighted_mean": 0.8789, "tension_weighted_mean": 0.9467}, "hypertrophic_quality_ratio": 0.9467, "active_tension_exposure_sum_cm2": 129.33}	{"obliques": 0.9500, "brachialis": 0.9500, "rotator_cuffs": 1.0000, "wrist_flexors": 0.9500, "biceps_brachii": 0.9500, "erector_spinae": 0.9500, "brachioradialis": 0.9500, "deltoid_lateral": 0.9500, "trapezius_lower": 0.9500, "trapezius_upper": 0.9500, "wrist_extensors": 0.9500, "deltoid_anterior": 1.0500, "pectoralis_minor": 0.9500, "trapezius_middle": 0.9500, "serratus_anterior": 0.9500, "pronators_supinators": 0.9500, "transverse_abdominis": 0.9500, "pectoralis_major_sternal": 1.1000, "pectoralis_major_clavicular": 1.1000}	{"slug": "single_arm_low_to_high_cable_fly", "notes": ["The fly's single-joint resistance profile combined with constant cable tension is the identifiable mechanism: peak moment arm coincides with maximal horizontal abduction, so the pectoral fibres resist high force at near-maximal length during the eccentric.", "Both pectoral heads receive 1.10 here, unlike the high-to-low variant where only the sternal head was elevated — the ascending arc means the clavicular fibres are the ones lengthened at peak resistance rather than shortened.", "Rotator cuffs were placed at the reference rather than 0.95 because a single-arm cable has no fixed path and demands active humeral trajectory control, matching the treatment given to free-weight pressing.", "Elbow flexors were assigned 0.95 because in a fly they hold a fixed angle isometrically rather than moving through a loaded range — the opposite of their role in rowing or pulldown patterns.", "Eccentric structural stress and lengthened-position loading were combined into one mechanism per muscle rather than counted as two full penalties, capping values at 1.10."], "reconciliation": "PASS", "muscle_evaluation": [{"R_m": 1.1000, "muscle": "pectoralis_major_sternal", "rationale": "A single-joint fly places the peak resistance moment at maximal horizontal abduction, and the cable — unlike a dumbbell — maintains full tension throughout the stretched bottom position rather than unloading there. Peak active force therefore coincides with the pectoralis at near-maximal length during the eccentric, the same defining mechanism as the pec deck fly. The unilateral setup permits a slightly greater reach into abduction. Eccentric stress and lengthened-position loading are combined into one mechanism, capping the value at 1.10.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 53.48, "tension_fraction": 0.5813, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "substantial", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 31.09, "eccentric_structural_stress": "emphasized", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "none", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["high_force_active_lengthening_at_maximally_abducted_shoulder", "cable_maintaining_full_resistance_in_the_stretched_position"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "pronounced"}, {"R_m": 1.0500, "muscle": "deltoid_anterior", "rationale": "The low-to-high path recruits it strongly as a shoulder flexor, and the bottom position holds it under cable tension at an extended, abducted shoulder angle. This mild high-force lengthening plus a tension fraction of 0.69 justifies a small elevation, kept below the pectoralis because it bears a smaller share of the end-range moment.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 30.46, "tension_fraction": 0.6921, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "high", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 21.08, "eccentric_structural_stress": "standard", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "none", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["loaded_eccentric_at_extended_abducted_shoulder", "high_relative_tension_nonlinear_residual"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "mild"}, {"R_m": 1.0000, "muscle": "rotator_cuffs", "rationale": "A single-arm cable fly has no fixed path, so the cuff must actively control humeral head position and internal rotation through an unguided arc against a constant line of pull, rather than passively centring against a machine track. This dynamic control places it at the reference rather than the sub-reference value used for machine-supported stabilization.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 170.80, "tension_fraction": 0.0908, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 15.50, "eccentric_structural_stress": "standard", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "none", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["conventional_contractile_fatigue"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 1.1000, "muscle": "pectoralis_major_clavicular", "rationale": "The ascending low-to-high arc preferentially recruits the clavicular fibres, and the cable holds full tension as they lengthen toward the bottom abducted position. Unlike the high-to-low variant where these fibres are shortened at peak resistance, here they are the ones exposed to the loaded stretch, so they share the sternal head's elevation rather than sitting at the reference. A tension fraction of 0.77 adds a small nonlinear residual.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 13.52, "tension_fraction": 0.7692, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "high", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 10.40, "eccentric_structural_stress": "emphasized", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "none", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["high_force_active_lengthening_at_maximally_abducted_shoulder", "high_relative_tension_nonlinear_residual"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "pronounced"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "brachialis", "rationale": "Holds a fixed slightly-flexed elbow angle against the cable throughout the arc rather than moving through a loaded range; the tension is positional and non-lengthening, so the fatigue generated is largely transient.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 44.05, "tension_fraction": 0.2104, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "moderate", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 9.27, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "moderate", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["low_level_positional_isometric_tension"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "biceps_brachii", "rationale": "Maintains the fixed elbow angle and assists shoulder flexion at low force without dynamic excursion; it is not resisting load at a lengthened position, so its persistent recovery component sits below the dynamic reference.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 39.81, "tension_fraction": 0.2035, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "moderate", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 8.10, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "moderate", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["low_level_positional_isometric_tension"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "serratus_anterior", "rationale": "Controls scapular position against the unilateral pull at submaximal force with no meaningful loaded lengthening; such stabilizing tension produces predominantly transient fatigue.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 36.03, "tension_fraction": 0.2082, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "moderate", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 7.50, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "moderate", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["low_level_scapular_stabilizing_tension"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "wrist_flexors", "rationale": "Grips the handle at submaximal isometric force with no lengthening under load and no meaningful perfusion restriction; the fatigue generated resolves rapidly.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 54.40, "tension_fraction": 0.0643, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 3.50, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "moderate", "domina