Centres the humeral head against traction from the suspended body and controls rotation as the shoulder moves from overhead elevation into adduction. A small increment reflects additional co-contraction near the top and bottom positions.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 170.80, "mechanical_roles": ["joint_stabilization", "load_transmission", "eccentric_control"], "tension_fraction": 0.0703, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 10.42, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile", "dynamic_eccentric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 12.00, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "trapezius_lower", "rationale": "Controls scapular depression, upward-rotation reversal, and posterior tilt while anchoring the scapula under bodyweight traction. A limited increment represents continuous fixation beyond the supplied dynamic contribution.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 14.98, "mechanical_roles": ["scapular_control", "load_transmission", "eccentric_control"], "tension_fraction": 0.7009, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 9.51, "contraction_character": ["dynamic_concentric", "dynamic_eccentric", "isometric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 10.50, "input_contribution_classification": "mixed_propulsive_and_stabilizing"}, {"muscle": "rectus_abdominis", "rationale": "Maintains the ribcage-pelvis relationship and limits lumbar extension or swinging while the body hangs beneath the bar. A small increment reflects continuous anti-extension demand.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 24.29, "mechanical_roles": ["trunk_bracing", "isometric_fixation", "limb_position_maintenance"], "tension_fraction": 0.2470, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 5.15, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 6.00, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "obliques", "rationale": "Resists trunk rotation and lateral deviation caused by small asymmetries in the wide grip and pulling force. A modest increment reflects