t-centring demand.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 170.80, "mechanical_roles": ["joint_stabilization", "load_transmission", "isometric_fixation", "multi_joint_control"], "tension_fraction": 0.0293, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 4.10, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 5.00, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "serratus_anterior", "rationale": "Maintains scapular upward rotation, posterior tilt, and thoracic contact while the upper arms stay overhead. A small increment reflects continuous scapular fixation.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 36.03, "mechanical_roles": ["scapular_control", "load_transmission", "isometric_fixation"], "tension_fraction": 0.0694, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 1.98, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.50, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "wrist_flexors", "rationale": "Maintains the rope grip and transmits cable force through the hands while resisting unwanted wrist extension.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 54.40, "mechanical_roles": ["grip_maintenance", "isometric_fixation", "load_transmission"], "tension_fraction": 0.0368, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.00, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "obliques", "rationale": "Resists trunk extension, rotation, and lateral deviation as the cable pulls the elevated arms posteriorly.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 81.71, "mechanical_roles": ["trunk_bracing", "antagonist_co_contraction", "isometric_fixation"], "tension_fraction": 0.0245, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.00, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "rectus_abdominis", "rationale": "Maintains ribcage-to-pelvis alignment and limits lumbar extension caused by the overhead arm position and cable line of pull.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 24.29, "mechanical_roles": ["trunk_bracing", "isometric_fixation", "load_transmission"], "tension_fraction": 0.0618, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.50, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "transverse_abdominis", "rationale": "Provides circumferential abdominal stiffness so cable force can be transmitted through the standing trunk without excessive spinal movement.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 21.97, "mechanical_roles": ["trunk_bracing", "isometric_fixation", "load_transmission"], "tension_fraction": 0.0683, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.50, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "wrist_extensors", "rationale": "Co-contracts with the wrist flexors to maintain stable wrist alignment while the rope separates during elbow extension.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 53.67, "mechanical_roles": ["grip_maintenance", "antagonist_co_contraction", "isometric_fixation"], "tension_fraction": 0.0279, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.50, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "trapezius_lower", "rationale": "Supports scapular posterior tilt and rotational balance while preventing uncontrolled elevation during the overhead hold.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 14.98, "mechanical_roles": ["scapular_control", "load_transmission", "isometric_fixation"], "tension_fraction": 0.0801, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.20, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "trapezius_upper", "rationale": "Stabilizes the clavicle and assists scapular upward-rotation balance while the arms remain elevated. The low value avoids interpreting the exercise as an active shrug.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 19.36, "mechanical_roles": ["scapular_control", "load_transmission", "isometric_fixation"], "tension_fraction": 0.0517, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.00, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}], "saturated_muscles": [], "standardized_repetition": {"tempo": "controlled conventional tempo", "execution_scope": "bilateral", "range_of_motion": "full intended ROM", "proximity_to_failure": "effective repetition"}, "tension_expansion_ratio": 1.1406, "propulsive_vector_sum_cm2": 88.79, "propulsive_fcsa_demand_cm2": 88.79, "active_tension_exposure_sum_cm2": 101.27}	{"obliques": 1.70, "rotator_cuffs": 4.00, "wrist_flexors": 1.70, "trapezius_lower": 1.02, "trapezius_upper": 0.85, "wrist_extensors": 1.28, "deltoid_anterior": 5.53, "rectus_abdominis": 1.28, "serratus_anterior": 2.13, "triceps_long_head": 43.63, "triceps_medial_head": 12.23, "transverse_abdominis": 1.20, "triceps_lateral_head": 28.33}	{"slug": "overhead_rope_triceps_extension", "notes": ["The triceps long head receives the largest modifier because shoulder elevation and deep elbow flexion create pronounced high-tension loading at a long muscle length.", "The lateral and medial heads receive smaller positive modifiers because continuous cable resistance loads them dynamically through broad elbow-extension ROM from a flexed starting position.", "The anterior deltoid, serratus anterior, grip, wrist, scapular, and abdominal contributions receive reduced modifiers because they are predominantly isometric or stabilizing.", "The rotator cuffs and transverse abdominis receive the minimum modifier because their exposure consists almost entirely of low-ROM joint stabilization or trunk bracing.", "ETU values equal active tension exposure multiplied by the listed H_m values within rounding tolerance."], "etu_sum_cm2": 104.86, "reconciliation": "PASS", "muscle_evaluation": [{"H_m": 1.1500, "muscle": "triceps_long_head", "etu_cm2": 43.63, "rationale": "The exercise combines very high recruitment with pronounced long-length loading, broad elbow-extension ROM, and continuous cable tension. This supports a strong positive modifier without implying specialized eccentric overload.", "normalized_etu": 1.0018, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric"], "high_tension_rom": "broad", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 43.55, "smh_interpretation": "Shoulder elevation lengthens the biarticular long head proximally while deep elbow flexion lengthens it distally, and cable resistance remains present through the full extension arc.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 37.94, "resistance_profile_alignment": "very_good", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "substantially_lengthened"}, {"H_m": 1.0500, "muscle": "triceps_lateral_head", "etu_cm2": 28.33, "rationale": "Broad dynamic elbow-extension loading from a flexed and lengthened starting position under continuous cable resistance supports a modest positive modifier.", "normalized_etu": 0.7848, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric"], "high_tension_rom": "broad", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 36.10, "smh_interpretation": "The elbow begins deeply flexed and extends through a broad range while cable tension remains comparatively continuous.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 26.98, "resistance_profile_alignment": "very_good", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "moderately_lengthened"}, {"H_m": 1.0500, "muscle": "triceps_medial_head", "etu_cm2": 12.23, "rationale": "Meaningful tension at the flexed-elbow start and broad controlled concentric-eccentric ROM support a mod